1
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:05,790
- Here you go.         - Thank you.

2
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:08,710
"Say, Rachel...

3
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:11,710
...I was wondering if you'd like to go to a movie with me sometime...

4
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:13,510
...as my lover."

5
00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:18,140
Mm. Too out there.

6
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,100
"Maybe you'd just like to get something to eat with me sometime...

7
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:23,480
...as my lover."

8
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:27,600
- Hi.     - Hi.

9
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:29,520
All right, let's go shopping.

10
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:32,400
You know, before we go, uh, there's something I need to say.

11
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:34,900
- Oh. Okay.     - Okay.

12
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:40,620
I've kind of had this, uh... This crush on you.

13
00:00:41,790 --> 00:00:44,660
But since you were with Ross, I didn't do anything about it.

14
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:48,790
Now that you're not, I'd really like to ask you out sometime.

15
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:53,340
So that's what I'm doing now.

16
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:10,360
I dropped a cup.

17
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,500
# So no one told you life was gonna be this way #

18
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:26,240
# Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. #

19
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:30,960
# It's like you're always stuck in second gear #

20
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,520
# When it hasn't been your day, #

21
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:36,520
# your week, your month, or even your year #

22
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:40,480
# but I'll be there for you #

23
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:42,310
# When the rain starts to pour #

24
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:45,430
# I'll be there for you #

25
00:01:45,430 --> 00:01:47,270
# Like I've been there before #

26
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:50,280
# I'll be there for you #

27
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:53,940
# 'Cause you're there for me too #

28
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:03,910
So that's why within a few years, that voice recognition...

29
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:06,250
...is gonna be pretty much standard on any computer.

30
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:11,130
You know, so you could be, like, "Wash my car. Clean my room."

31
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:13,380
It's not gonna be able to do any of those things...

32
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,460
...but it'll understand what you're saying.

33
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:20,050
- Oh, this was so great.     - Yeah, it was.

34
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:22,800
All right, then.

35
00:02:23,890 --> 00:02:25,390
Bye.

36
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:33,690
Hello, people who do not live here.

37
00:02:34,570 --> 00:02:35,940
- Hi.     - Hello.

38
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:40,320
I gave you a key for emergencies.

39
00:02:40,490 --> 00:02:42,570
We were out of Doritos.

40
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:46,950
Hey, how'd the date go with Mr. Millionaire?

41
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:50,210
"Mr. Millionaire. New, from Snooty Playthings.

42
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,130
Third wife sold separately."

43
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,840
He's great. I mean, we have such a good time together.

44
00:02:57,010 --> 00:03:02,090
He's so funny and so sweet. And I'm not attracted to him at all.

45
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:04,300
- Still?     - No.

46
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:08,270
It's driving me crazy. I mean, in every other way, he's like the perfect guy.

47
00:03:08,430 --> 00:03:12,350
He has everything. Plus, he actually has everything.

48
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:16,270
Life-sized lmperial Storm Troopers from Sharper lmage?

49
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:17,820
Two.

50
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:20,570
Wow. Can Joey and I put them on and fight?

51
00:03:22,950 --> 00:03:31,790
Oh, Mommy. Oh, Daddy. I am a big old baddy.

52
00:03:35,630 --> 00:03:38,090
I guess he must've gotten the part in that play.

53
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:41,220
Either that or Gloria Estefan was right.

54
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:43,800
Eventually, the rhythm is going to get you.

55
00:03:46,850 --> 00:03:48,430

56
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:52,270
- Joe, how's it going?     - Good.

57
00:03:56,690 --> 00:03:58,610
- Hey.     - Hi.

58
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:01,070
Ah, so you're playing Adrianne, huh?

59
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:03,780
Yes. Are you one of the retarded cousins?

60
00:04:05,950 --> 00:04:09,660
No, no. Uh, I'm playing your husband, Victor. I'm Joey Tribbiani.

61
00:04:09,830 --> 00:04:12,040
Hi. Nice to meet you. Kate Miller.

62
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:21,590
Heh. So the, uh, play's pretty great, huh?

63
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:24,340
Oh, yeah. I love Jennifer Banberry's work.

64
00:04:24,510 --> 00:04:25,760
She's so brilliantly incisive...

65
00:04:25,930 --> 00:04:28,640
...when it comes to deconstructing the psyche of the middle class.

66
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:31,850
Oh, forget about it. She rocks. Ha, ha.

67
00:04:36,690 --> 00:04:38,860
Where do I know you from?

68
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:42,530
Dr. Drake Ramoray?

69
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:45,150
Days of our Lives?

70
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:48,070
Voted most datable neurosurgeon by Teen Beat?

71
00:04:49,370 --> 00:04:51,290
No, that's not it.

72
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:53,830
So you're a soap actor.

73
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:57,290
Well, this must be exciting for you, being in a real play. Hmm?

74
00:04:57,500 --> 00:05:00,290
Hey, I've done plays before. I'm a serious actor.

75
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:02,840
That infomercial.

76
00:05:05,130 --> 00:05:07,010
For the milk-carton-spout thing.

77
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:09,930
You're the guy who doesn't know how to pour milk.

78
00:05:11,390 --> 00:05:14,890
See, I actually can pour milk. But I got you believing that I couldn't.

79
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:17,560
Ha, ha. Now, see, that's acting.

80
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:21,060
Right. At the end, you choked on a cookie.

81
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:22,940
Yeah, that was real.

82
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:27,990
- Wow. I cannot believe Mark asked you out.     - I know.

83
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,950
Well, So, what are you gonna tell him?

84
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:34,160
Well, I told him I would think about it, but I'm gonna tell him no.

85
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:39,420
I mean, I think I'd say no to anybody right now.

86
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:45,670
Oh, but it was so strange. I mean, I'm standing there...

87
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:50,090
...with this charming, cute guy who's asking me to go out with him...

88
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:52,010
...which I'm allowed to do...

89
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:56,480
...and I felt guilty, you know, like I'd be cheating on Ross or something.

90
00:05:57,060 --> 00:06:00,190
Wow. So, okay, maybe that means...

91
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:04,320
...that you're not over Ross yet and you have issues with your father.

92
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:10,120
I don't have any issues with my father.

93
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:12,120
Okay, so it's probably just the Ross thing.

94
00:06:14,410 --> 00:06:16,410
I hate this woman. I hate her.

95
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:19,210
She told everyone in the company about that infomercial...

96
00:06:19,370 --> 00:06:22,460
...and now they all keep asking me to open their drinks.

97
00:06:22,630 --> 00:06:27,010
Okay? And whenever I can't do it, they're all, like, laughing at me.

98
00:06:29,930 --> 00:06:32,300
- Hello.     - Hey.

99
00:06:32,470 --> 00:06:34,430
So Rachel called.

100
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:37,140
Wants to see me.

101
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:40,020
Going over in a minute.

102
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:45,070
- Wow. What do you think she wants?     - Well, maybe the crazy fog has lifted...

103
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:48,490
...and she realizes that life without me...

104
00:06:48,650 --> 00:06:49,650
...sucks.

105
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:55,830
It's possible. You are very lovable. I'd miss you if I broke up with you.

106
00:06:56,910 --> 00:06:58,660
Just trying to be supportive.

107
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:01,670
Well, be supportive like a guy.

108
00:07:02,830 --> 00:07:05,040
If I broke up with you, I'd miss you.

109
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:11,510
- Hi.     - Hi.

110
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:15,720
You, uh, wanted to see me?

111
00:07:18,470 --> 00:07:19,850
Yeah.

112
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:23,440
Uh, here's a box of your stuff.

113
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:29,610
- What?     - Uh, it's just like hats and a shirt and CD's.

114
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:32,030
Just sort of stuff that you've left here.

115
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:35,280
What are you doing? Are you trying to hurt me or something?

116
00:07:38,790 --> 00:07:40,290
Ross.

117
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:45,540
It just seems that, you know, it's time we, you know, move on.

118
00:07:45,710 --> 00:07:47,210
I mean, don't you think?

119
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:50,630
- Yes.     - Yeah.

120
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,380
- Yes, I do.     - Good.

121
00:07:52,550 --> 00:07:54,630
Yeah, I really do.

122
00:07:56,050 --> 00:07:57,550
Hey...

123
00:07:57,890 --> 00:08:00,470
This was a gift.

124
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:03,640
Ross, you got that for free from the museum gift shop.

125
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,770
It's still a gift.

126
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:08,480
I got it from the gift shop.

127
00:08:10,150 --> 00:08:12,360
Okay. All right. Give me the mug. I'll keep the mug.

128
00:08:12,530 --> 00:08:16,620
No. You know, don't do me any favors. In fact, where...

129
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:21,160
Where's the rest of my stuff? Huh? Like my, um...

130
00:08:21,330 --> 00:08:24,660
Hey. This book is mine.

131
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:31,090
And that T-shirt you sleep in? I'd like that back too. Yes, I do.

132
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:37,430
You know how much I love that T-shirt. You never even wear that T-shirt.

133
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:40,720
I'm just trying to help you move on.

134
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:43,980
Oh, you are a petty man.

135
00:08:44,140 --> 00:08:46,270
You are a petty, petty...

136
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:47,900
- Petty...     - ...petty, petty...

137
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:49,360
- ...small...      - ...small...

138
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:55,570
You are so just doing this out of spite.

139
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:57,570
Uh-uh. No, no, no.

140
00:08:57,740 --> 00:09:00,870
I'm gonna wear this all the time. I love this shirt.

141
00:09:01,450 --> 00:09:05,410
You haven't worn that since you were 15. It doesn't even fit you anymore.

142
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:07,960
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.     - Yeah, yeah.

143
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:10,540
Oh, okay, okay, okay.

144
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:17,960

145
00:09:21,890 --> 00:09:25,310
Now, if you don't mind, I'm gonna take the rest of my stuff...

146
00:09:25,810 --> 00:09:27,850
...and relax...

147
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:30,940
...in my favorite shirt.

148
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:35,030
You have a pleasant evening.

149
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,620
So you're, like, a zillionaire.

150
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:50,750
And you're our age. You're our age.

151
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:54,000
You know what? You should, like, buy a state...

152
00:09:54,170 --> 00:09:56,550
...and then just name it after yourself.

153
00:09:57,130 --> 00:09:58,510
What, like, "Pete Dakota"?

154
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:01,850
Or "Mississi-Pete."

155
00:10:03,430 --> 00:10:06,680
Ooh, ooh, I got it: "Pete Chicago."

156
00:10:08,310 --> 00:10:10,270
That's not a state, Joe.

157
00:10:10,690 --> 00:10:13,110
Oh, and "Mississi-Pete" is?

158
00:10:15,190 --> 00:10:18,530
I gotta go, so, uh, I'll see you guys later.

159
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:21,030
- Okay. You're our age.     - Okay.

160
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:24,950
So, uh, are we on for tomorrow?

161
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:26,790
Absolutely.

162
00:10:28,330 --> 00:10:30,670
Now get out of here, you.

163
00:10:36,710 --> 00:10:39,800
Okay, I'm running out of places I can touch him.

164
00:10:40,470 --> 00:10:42,050
Is there something wrong with me?

165
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:45,010
I mean, why am I only attracted to guys where there's no future?

166
00:10:45,180 --> 00:10:47,810
Either they're too old or they're too young.

167
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:50,140
And there's Pete, who's crazy about me...

168
00:10:50,390 --> 00:10:53,730
...and he's absolutely perfect, and there's, like, zip going on.

169
00:10:53,980 --> 00:10:56,270
Seriously. Does it sound like something's wrong with me?

170
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:58,230
Yeah, kind of.

171
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:03,910
Happy? Is that what I'm supposed to be, Vic?

172
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,450
Happy?

173
00:11:05,620 --> 00:11:08,200
Well, why don't you tell me what you're supposed to be? Huh?

174
00:11:08,370 --> 00:11:10,830
Because I sure as hell can't figure it out.

175
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,420
I talk to you, and nothing.

176
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:16,040
You look at me, and it's nothing.

177
00:11:19,170 --> 00:11:20,420
Nothing.

178
00:11:23,050 --> 00:11:24,180
Tasty.

179
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:30,020
I'm really starting to feel like you guys have a history. It's nice.

180
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:32,520
- I have a question about this scene.     - Yes.

181
00:11:32,690 --> 00:11:37,110
Well, I don't understand why Adrianne's attracted to Victor.

182
00:11:37,270 --> 00:11:39,780
Peel the onion.

183
00:11:40,150 --> 00:11:42,200
First of all, he's good-looking.

184
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:46,950
I think my character is gonna need a bit more of a reason than that.

185
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:50,370
Oh, hey, how about this one? Uh, it says so in the script.

186
00:11:53,290 --> 00:11:56,290
You know, I don't know why my character likes you either.

187
00:11:56,460 --> 00:11:59,460
I mean, it says in the script here that you're a bitch.

188
00:12:00,170 --> 00:12:02,920
- It doesn't say that in the script.     - It does in mine.

189
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:09,310
I can blow-dry it, I can put gel on it. It doesn't matter.

190
00:12:09,470 --> 00:12:12,310
I still wind up with this little cowlick-y thing...

191
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:16,060
...on the middle part of my head. It's so annoying.

192
00:12:16,230 --> 00:12:18,230
- Does it bug you?     - You bug me.

193
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:34,500
Is there any chance you didn't see that?

194
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,210
Ross, you gotta stop, okay?

195
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:43,340
You can't just stare through the peephole for three hours.

196
00:12:46,010 --> 00:12:47,680
You're gonna get peep-eye.

197
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:51,680
I knew it. I knew it. I always knew she liked him.

198
00:12:52,060 --> 00:12:54,020
She'd say no, but here we are, right?

199
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:56,640
We just broke up, first thing she does.

200
00:12:56,850 --> 00:12:58,400
You didn't just break up.

201
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:00,520
Hey, it's been, like, three weeks.

202
00:13:00,730 --> 00:13:04,070
You slept with somebody three hours after you thought you broke up.

203
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:07,240
I mean, bullets have left guns slower.

204
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:10,740
Here they come. Here they... Oh.

205
00:13:10,910 --> 00:13:13,660
If she kisses him good night, I'm gonna kill myself. I swear.

206
00:13:13,830 --> 00:13:15,870
I can't watch.

207
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:18,670
Come on. Date over. Date over.

208
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:22,210
- Here we go. She's going in.     - Okay.

209
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:25,090
She's going in. Ha, ha. Wait. He's going in.

210
00:13:26,930 --> 00:13:28,550
He's going in.

211
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:32,560
The door's closed. I can't see anything with the door closed.

212
00:13:32,890 --> 00:13:36,560
And the inventor of the door rests happily in his grave.

213
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:39,440
Okay, I have to do something. I mean, I have to stop it.

214
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:41,190
- Stop what?     - I don't know.

215
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:44,400
But I have a feeling that my being there will do it.

216
00:13:44,610 --> 00:13:47,150
I'll go over and I will borrow something.

217
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:49,070
- Juice. I need juice.     - No.

218
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:50,570
- You can't.     - A little help.

219
00:13:51,410 --> 00:13:53,580
- They must be stopped.     - I am your friend...

220
00:13:53,740 --> 00:13:55,790
...and I am not gonna let you do this.

221
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:58,500
You are surprisingly strong.

222
00:13:59,210 --> 00:14:02,750
- I need juice. People need juice.     - Look, man...

223
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:05,840
- People need juice. Juice. They need...     - Listen to me.

224
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:13,970
She's moving on, okay? If it's not this guy, it's gonna be somebody else.

225
00:14:14,140 --> 00:14:16,470
And unless you're thinking about subletting my peephole...

226
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:20,650
...you are gonna have to get used to the fact that the relationship is over.

227
00:14:20,810 --> 00:14:24,070
Okay, man? It's over.

228
00:14:27,030 --> 00:14:30,240
- Yeah, okay.     - Okay.

229
00:14:30,410 --> 00:14:32,950
It's just I miss her so much.

230
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:35,660
I know.

231
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:40,370
Why do all your coffee mugs have numbers on the bottom?

232
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:43,420
Oh, that's so Monica can keep track.

233
00:14:43,590 --> 00:14:47,380
That way, if one of them is missing, she can be like, "Where's number 27?"

234
00:14:56,350 --> 00:14:57,520
You know what?

235
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:00,310
No, and I don't think I'm gonna want to.

236
00:15:00,810 --> 00:15:01,850
I can't do this.

237
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:04,560
Yep. Yep. That's what I didn't want to know.

238
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:08,400
Yeah. Oh, Mark, I'm just doing this for the wrong reasons, you know?

239
00:15:08,570 --> 00:15:11,110
I'm just doing it to get back at Ross.

240
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:14,490
I'm sorry. It's not very fair to you.

241
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:18,620
Ah. Fair, shmair. You know?

242
00:15:18,790 --> 00:15:21,710
Look, you wanna get back at Ross, I am here for you.

243
00:15:23,330 --> 00:15:24,420
Really.

244
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:29,590
No, no. I say we get back at him right here on this couch. Right here.

245
00:15:31,090 --> 00:15:33,470
Oh, my God.

246
00:15:34,930 --> 00:15:36,390
I'm sorry about this.

247
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,470
That's okay.

248
